  { id: '189', name: 'Vanuatu', capital: 'Port Vila', population: '326K', region: 'Oceania', flag: '🇻🇺', lat: -17.7333, lng: 168.3273, description: 'This South Pacific archipelago of roughly 80 islands ranks among the world\'s most culturally and linguistically diverse nations per capita, with over 100 indigenous languages spoken. Vanuatu is home to some of the most accessible active volcanoes on Earth, including Mount Yasur on Tanna, which has erupted nearly continuously for centuries. Its traditional land-diving ritual from Pentecost Island inspired modern bungee jumping.', area: '12.2K', currency: 'Vatu', languages: ['Bislama', 'English', 'French'], borders: [], gdp: '$980M', timeZone: 'UTC+11', callingCode: '+678', driveSide: 'Right' },
  { id: '190', name: 'Vatican City', capital: 'Vatican City', population: '800', region: 'Europe', flag: '🇻🇦', lat: 41.9029, lng: 12.4534, description: 'The world\'s smallest independent state at just 44 hectares, Vatican City serves as the spiritual and administrative center of the Roman Catholic Church and the residence of the Pope. Enclosed entirely within Rome, it houses extraordinary artistic treasures including Michelangelo\'s Sistine Chapel ceiling and St. Peter\'s Basilica, one of the largest churches ever built. Despite its tiny size, it maintains diplomatic relations with most of the world\'s nations.', area: '0.44', currency: 'Euro', languages: ['Italian', 'Latin'], borders: ['Italy'], gdp: '$0', timeZone: 'UTC+1', callingCode: '+39', driveSide: 'Right' },
  { id: '191', name: 'Venezuela', capital: 'Caracas', population: '28.3M', region: 'South America', flag: '🇻🇪', lat: 10.4806, lng: -66.9036, description: 'Blessed with the world\'s largest proven oil reserves and extraordinary natural wonders, Venezuela stretches from Caribbean beaches to Andean peaks and Amazonian rainforest. Angel Falls, plunging 979 meters from a tabletop mountain in Canaima National Park, is the world\'s highest uninterrupted waterfall. The country\'s diverse ecosystems harbor remarkable biodiversity, including the unique tepui formations that inspired Arthur Conan Doyle\'s The Lost World.', area: '916K', currency: 'Bolívar', languages: ['Spanish'], borders: ['Colombia', 'Brazil', 'Guyana'], gdp: '$92B', timeZone: 'UTC-4', callingCode: '+58', driveSide: 'Right' },
  { id: '192', name: 'Vietnam', capital: 'Hanoi', population: '98.1M', region: 'Asia', flag: '🇻🇳', lat: 21.0285, lng: 105.8542, description: 'Stretching along the eastern edge of the Indochinese Peninsula, Vietnam is shaped by a turbulent history that spans a thousand years of Chinese rule, French colonization, and wars that defined the 20th century. Today it is one of Southeast Asia\'s fastest-growing economies, renowned for its distinctive cuisine featuring pho and banh mi. From the terraced rice paddies of Sapa to Ha Long Bay\'s limestone karsts, its landscapes are breathtaking.', area: '331K', currency: 'Dong', languages: ['Vietnamese'], borders: ['China', 'Laos', 'Cambodia'], gdp: '$408B', timeZone: 'UTC+7', callingCode: '+84', driveSide: 'Right' },
  
  // --- Y ---
  { id: '193', name: 'Yemen', capital: 'Sana\'a', population: '33.7M', region: 'Asia', flag: '🇾🇪', lat: 15.3694, lng: 44.1910, description: 'Perched at the southwestern corner of the Arabian Peninsula, Yemen boasts a civilizational history stretching back millennia, including the legendary ancient Kingdom of Sheba. The old city of Sana\'a features remarkable multi-story mud-brick towers that represent one of the world\'s oldest examples of urban planning. The isolated island of Socotra harbors otherworldly flora, including the iconic dragon blood tree found nowhere else on Earth.', area: '527K', currency: 'Yemeni rial', languages: ['Arabic'], borders: ['Saudi Arabia', 'Oman'], gdp: '$21B', timeZone: 'UTC+3', callingCode: '+967', driveSide: 'Right' },
  
  // --- Z ---
  { id: '194', name: 'Zambia', capital: 'Lusaka', population: '20M', region: 'Africa', flag: '🇿🇲', lat: -15.3875, lng: 28.3228, description: 'Landlocked in southern Africa, Zambia shares with Zimbabwe one of the world\'s most awe-inspiring natural spectacles: Victoria Falls, known locally as Mosi-oa-Tunya, or The Smoke That Thunders. The country\'s vast wilderness areas, including South Luangwa National Park, pioneered the concept of walking safaris. Rich in copper deposits that drive its economy, Zambia is also known for its peaceful post-independence history and political stability.', area: '752K', currency: 'Zambian kwacha', languages: ['English'], borders: ['DR Congo', 'Tanzania', 'Malawi', 'Mozambique', 'Zimbabwe', 'Botswana', 'Namibia', 'Angola'], gdp: '$29B', timeZone: 'UTC+2', callingCode: '+260', driveSide: 'Left' },
  { id: '195', name: 'Zimbabwe', capital: 'Harare', population: '16.3M', region: 'Africa', flag: '🇿🇼', lat: -17.8216, lng: 31.0492, description: 'Home to the ancient stone city of Great Zimbabwe, whose impressive ruins gave the nation its name, this southern African country carries a heritage stretching back to powerful medieval trading kingdoms. Victoria Falls on its western border creates one of the continent\'s most dramatic natural landmarks. The country\'s diverse landscapes support abundant wildlife, from Hwange\'s elephant herds to Mana Pools\' painted dogs along the Zambezi River.', area: '390K', currency: 'US Dollar', languages: ['English', 'Shona', 'Ndebele'], borders: ['Zambia', 'Mozambique', 'South Africa', 'Botswana'], gdp: '$28B', timeZone: 'UTC+2', callingCode: '+263', driveSide: 'Left' }
